# Accepted findings for the container image scan (#476, policy in #474).
#
# Both image scans (build-and-push-image.yml before publishing, image-scan.yml weekly) read this
# file. An entry hides a vulnerability from the SARIF report and from the gate that blocks a release.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#
#   <ID> exp:<YYYY-MM-DD>  # <reason>
#
# - <ID> is the vulnerability ID Trivy reports (for example a CVE ID).
# - exp: is mandatory. On and after that date the entry stops applying and the finding is reported
#   again, so an accepted finding is reviewed instead of being hidden forever.
# - The reason is mandatory and says why the finding is accepted, with the issue that tracks it.
# - Entries are decided by the maintainer. The workflows fail if an entry lacks exp: or a reason.

CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31  # XsltView is not used; no 6.2.x fix, only Spring Framework 7.0.9 (#488)
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31  # Not exploitable while the app has no SSE or fragment rendering; no 6.2.x fix; see #488. Re-evaluate before #162 adds SSE.
